# Search (male)
# hardware/male/search/__init__.py - started by Male.loop() when a male becomes unsatisfied. Owns and starts Blink - expanded inline below (its own concurrent clock, starting the instant that line fires).

0 setup(): starts blink (started_by=self)
-> thread-blink
0 loop(): if the male isn't currently moving, call toggle_position() - same min/max sway every other body uses
0 ~ male reaches max/min position, then reverses on the next idle tick - repeats indefinitely
0 setdown(): logs only - doesn't explicitly stop blink; blink stops itself on its own next tick once it notices Search (its started_by) is no longer running (base_thread's break condition)
0 nothing in this thread (or in Male.loop()) re-checks is_satisfied() once running - it keeps sweeping and blinking until Male.setdown() forces search.stop() (SCENARIOS.md 1.2)
